---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE, FRAMING } from '../data/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Shengyi Wei is a digital design and computer architecture engineer working on AI data movement, memory systems, interconnects and RTL."
>
  <h1>About</h1>

  <div class="prose" style="margin-top:1.25rem">
    <p>
      I am <strong>{SITE.name}</strong>, a digital design and computer architecture engineer. My
      work sits around AI data movement: memory systems, interconnects and network-on-chip,
      workload-driven performance modeling, simulation, and RTL.
    </p>
    <p>{FRAMING}</p>
    <p>
      In practice that means starting from what a model actually does to memory, rather than from a
      block diagram, and carrying that measurement forward — into a model of the memory system and
      the interconnect, and then into hardware that the model justifies.
    </p>
    <p>
      This site is deliberately small. <a href="/projects">Projects</a> lists what is in progress
      and is honest about what is not built yet. <a href="/notes">Notes</a> will collect English
      technical write-ups. The <a href="/archive/zh">Chinese archive</a> preserves sixteen posts
      from the earlier version of this site, on PCIe, ASIC synthesis, RTL coding style and GPU
      microarchitecture.
    </p>
  </div>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <dl class="contact-grid">
      <dt>Email</dt>
      <dd><a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a></dd>
      <dt>GitHub</dt>
      <dd><a href={SITE.github}>github.com/hard-won</a></dd>
      {
        SITE.links.map((link) => (
          <>
            <dt>{link.label}</dt>
            <dd>
              <a href={link.href}>{link.href.replace(/^https?:\/\//, '')}</a>
            </dd>
          </>
        ))
      }
    </dl>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
